From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] leave the console alone

On quitting, Qt's VT handler switches the text cursor of the console
back on (a blinking cursor top left over neutrino's OSD) and sets
screen blanking to 15 minutes. neutrino owns the console.
---
diff --git a/main.cpp b/main.cpp
index 6fb7006..ef44522 100644
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -71,6 +71,10 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
         qputenv("QT_QPA_EGLFS_WIDTH", QByteArray::number(EGLFS_DEFAULT_WIDTH));
     if (qgetenv("QT_QPA_EGLFS_HEIGHT").isNull())
         qputenv("QT_QPA_EGLFS_HEIGHT", QByteArray::number(EGLFS_DEFAULT_HEIGHT));
+    // neutrino owns the console: Qt would switch its text cursor back on and
+    // set up screen blanking when the browser quits
+    if (qgetenv("QT_QPA_PRESERVE_CONSOLE_STATE").isNull())
+        qputenv("QT_QPA_PRESERVE_CONSOLE_STATE", "1");
     // the browser runs as root, where chromium refuses its sandbox
     if (qgetenv("QTWEBENGINE_DISABLE_SANDBOX").isNull())
         qputenv("QTWEBENGINE_DISABLE_SANDBOX", "1");
